:: Doctor Harper Autism Check-up
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>>
<<harper_intro>>
Harper takes a blank form from the drawer and turns <<his>> chair to face you.
"Tell me what made you ask about this."
<br><br>
You start with the sounds. Some of them stop your thinking outright, and you have to wait for them to end before
you can find the thought again. Harper writes without looking down at the page. When you stop talking,
<<he>> asks what school is like, then work, then what happens when someone changes a plan on you at the last minute.
<br><br>
You are still answering when <<he>> reaches back to the shelf behind <<him>> for a thin folder.
<br><br>
Harper turns the folder to face you and marks three lines with <<his>> pen. "Your answers fit Autism Spectrum.
It changes how you sort what comes in, and how fast you can leave one task for another.
The part that keeps you on one subject for six hours is the same part that costs you so much when someone interrupts."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Doctor Harper Autism Check-up 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Doctor Harper Autism Check-up 2
<<effects>>
<<He>> taps the paragraph about your fixation. "Learn where the practice stops paying you back.
Eat, wash, sleep, then start again the next day. Keep the sessions short while you're worn down."
<br><br>
<<if $harper_appointments.enabled>>
	<<He>> closes the folder. "You already see me on Fridays. Write your questions down and bring them,
	and don't skip the appointment because something else has your interest that week."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> signs the last page, slides the report into a document wallet and pushes it across the desk to you.
	<span class="green">Harper gives you documentation explaining your condition.</span>
	<<set $autismSpectrum.harperDiscussed to true>><<set $autismSpectrum.documentation to true>>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Return to the foyer|Hospital Foyer]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	Harper leaves the appointment page open on <<his>> computer. "I can see you properly, once a week, here,
	on Fridays. Shall I put you down?"
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Agree to the weekly check-up|Doctor Harper Autism Appointment]]>><<set $harper_appointments.enabled to true>><<unset $schoolPsych>><<set $autismSpectrum.harperDiscussed to true>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Decline|Doctor Harper Autism Decline]]>><<set $autismSpectrum.harperDiscussed to true>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>

:: Doctor Harper Autism Appointment
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>>
Harper types your name into the appointment list, then checks the time twice before saving it.
<br><br>
"Friday," <<he>> says, writing the day on a card in letters big enough to read from across a room.
"Come to the foyer and follow the sign to my office. Keep this with the report so you find both at once."
<br><br>
<<if $autismSpectrum.documentation>>
	<<He>> holds out the card for you to clip to the report you already carry.
<<else>>
	<<He>> signs the last page, slides the report into a document wallet and hands you the wallet with the card on top.
	<span class="green">You now have documentation explaining your condition.</span>
	<<set $autismSpectrum.documentation to true>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if Time.weekDay is 6 and $daily.harperVisit isnot 1>>
	Harper looks at the clock. "You've saved yourself a walk. It's Friday, so we can start now."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Begin today's check-up|Doctor Harper's Office]]>><<set $daily.harperVisit to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Return to the foyer|Hospital Foyer]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Doctor Harper Autism Appointment Later
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>>
<<harper_intro>>
You tell Harper you have changed your mind about the weekly appointment. <<He>> opens the list on <<his>>
computer without asking what changed.
<br><br>
"You said you might," <<he>> says.
<br><br>
<<link [[Book it|Doctor Harper Autism Appointment]]>><<set $harper_appointments.enabled to true>><<unset $schoolPsych>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Change your mind again|Doctor Harper Autism Decline]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Doctor Harper Autism Decline
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "hospital">><<effects>>
You tell Harper you don't want another weekly appointment. <<He>> draws a line through the open form
and closes it without asking why.
<br><br>
"Ask me again whenever you like. The offer stays open. Come to the foyer and say so."
<<if $autismSpectrum.documentation>>
	<<He>> nods at the wallet you already carry. "Nothing in the report changes because you turned this down."
<<else>>
	<<He>> signs the report and turns it around so you can read the first page. "This says what we went through today.
	Hand it over on the days when saying it yourself is too much work." Harper slides it into a document wallet and
	gives it to you. <span class="green">You now have documentation explaining your condition.</span>
	<<set $autismSpectrum.documentation to true>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Return to the foyer|Hospital Foyer]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Documentation
<<effects>><<set $autismSpectrum.kylarDiscussed to true>>
You take Harper's wallet out of your bag and tell Kylar where it came from. <<He>> reaches for it,
stops with <<his>> hand halfway there, and rubs both palms down <<his>> clothes before trying again.
<br><br>
"May I?" <<he>> asks.
<br><br>
You hand it over. Kylar sits and spreads the wallet across <<his>> knees. <<He>> reads the heading,
turns to the second page, then goes back to the heading and reads it again.
<br><br>
"Harper wrote this. About you." <<He>> shuts the wallet and holds it flat against <<his>> sketchbook.
"I have Autism as well. There are reports at home. M-My... parents kept every one of them."
<br><br>
<<link [[Tell Kylar about Harper's questions|Kylar Autism Documentation Harper]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask how Autism affects <<him>>|Kylar Autism Documentation Kylar]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Documentation Harper
<<effects>>
You go through what Harper asked you. Noise. Routines. The way one subject can take a whole week.
Kylar finds each of them on the page as you say it, dragging one finger down the report to keep <<his>> place.
<br><br>
"Yeah. The bell hurts," <<he>> says. "I know when it's coming. That doesn't help.
I count the seconds down so it lands where I put it, and if anyone talks to me while I'm counting I have to start
the count again."
<br><br>
You tell <<him>> which sounds do that to you. Kylar turns to face you so fast that the report slides off <<his>> knees.
You both grab for it, and <<his>> hand closes over yours on the page. <<He>> leaves it there until footsteps
come up the path, then pulls back and smooths the paper flat.
<br><br>
<<include "Kylar Autism Documentation Offer">>

:: Kylar Autism Documentation Kylar
<<effects>>
Kylar opens <<his>> sketchbook to a page of drawings of the rear courtyard.
The same stump appears six times from six angles. You are in all six.
<br><br>
"Drawing is easier than talking, because I choose where everything goes," <<he>> says. <<He>>
turns forward a few pages to a map of the school with times written next to the doors.
"I walk the same way every day. I know four other ways. If I change halfway through I lose track of what I was doing."
<br><br>
You point at a route that runs between two classrooms you use. Kylar puts <<his>> palm flat over it.
<br><br>
"That one's only safe when you're with me," <<he>> says, and leaves <<his>> hand there until you go back to the report.
<br><br>
You ask whether that one is on the report too.
<br><br>
Kylar takes <<his>> hand off the map and looks at it.
<br><br>
"No," <<he>> says. "The walking is. The counting is. The bell. Harper could write those down about me and
it'd be the same words <<he>> used about you." <<He>> sets one finger next to the route instead of on it.
"This is something else. I know where you go because I worked it out, and I kept working it out,
and nobody made me do it. Y-You can put it on a different page from the rest if you like."
<br><br>
<<He>> doesn't say anything after that, and <<he>> doesn't move <<his>> finger either.
<br><br>
<<include "Kylar Autism Documentation Offer">>

:: Kylar Autism Documentation Offer [nobr]
Kylar finds the line about your current fixation and reads it twice.
"<span class="gold"><<= autismKylarTrainingName()>></span>," <<he>> says. "That's what's had you all week."
<br><br>
You tell <<him>> what you've been working on. Kylar slides your report inside <<his>> sketchbook to keep the pages flat,
then stands up with the whole bundle held against <<his>> chest.
<br><br>
"Take me with you," <<he>> says. "You can show me how it's done. I'll keep everyone else off you while you do it."
<br><br>
None of that last part is in the report. Kylar holds the bundle against <<his>> chest and waits.
<br><br>
<<link [[Train together|Kylar Autism Training Choice]]>><<npcincr Kylar love 1>><<npcincr Kylar rage -1>><</link>><<glove>><<lksuspicion>>
<br>
<<link [[Decline|Kylar Autism Training Decline]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Training Return
<<effects>>
You tell Kylar you want to work on <span class="gold"><<= autismKylarTrainingName()>></span> today.
<<He>> shuts <<his>> sketchbook, presses the pencils into their loop until they stop moving, and gets up.
<br><br>
"I remember last time," <<he>> says. "Tell me where before we set off. I don't want to find out at the corner."
<br><br>
<<link [[Choose a place|Kylar Autism Training Choice]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Change your mind|Kylar Autism Training Decline]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Training Decline
<<effects>>
You tell Kylar you don't want to train after all. <<His>> hand tightens on the edge of <<his>> sketchbook.
<<He>> looks down, opens it, and turns past the finished drawings until <<he>> reaches two blank pages facing each other.
<br><br>
"We could draw, then," <<he>> says, laying a pencil across the left-hand page for you. "Yours is yours.
I won't put anything on it unless you ask me to."
<br><br>
<<link [[Draw today's fixation together (0:30)|Kylar Autism Draw Fixation]]>><<pass 30>><<npcincr Kylar love 1>><<npcincr Kylar rage -1>><<stress -7>><</link>><<glove>><<lksuspicion>><<llstress>>
<br>
<<link [[Draw each other (0:30)|Kylar Autism Draw Portrait]]>><<pass 30>><<npcincr Kylar love 2>><<npcincr Kylar rage -3>><</link>><<gglove>><<llksuspicion>>
<br>
<<link [[Decline|Kylar Autism Return]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Draw Fixation
<<effects>><<run autismFinishKylarTraining()>>
You start with the part of <span class="gold"><<= autismKylarTrainingName()>></span> you keep coming back to.
Kylar watches your pencil for a while, then starts the same thing on <<his>> page from another angle.
<br><br>
Every time you add something <<he>> asks why it goes there, and your answer gives <<him>> the next thing to draw.
<br><br>
You rub out a line and put it back further left. Kylar copies the correction onto <<his>>
own page with a small arrow beside it, then keeps doing that for every change you make, until <<his>>
drawing has turned into a record of how you got there.
<br><br>
"Keep both of them," <<he>> says, tearing <<his>> page out slowly to leave a clean edge.
"You'll forget which parts were hard. Mine says which."
<br><br>
<<link [[Put the drawings away|Kylar Autism Return]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Draw Portrait
<<effects>><<run autismFinishKylarTraining()>>
You sit facing Kylar and start drawing.
<br><br>
<<He>> holds still while you look at <<him>>, then shuffles forward a few inches every time you look down at your page.
The fourth time, you tell <<him>> to go back. <<He>> measures the gap you point at and moves back exactly that far.
<br><br>
Kylar finishes well before you do. <<He>> has your clothes, your hair and the line of your mouth,
all of it drawn small. Your version of <<him>> is still missing a hand, because <<he>> keeps tucking
it under the sketchbook whenever you look for it.
<br><br>
"Draw it holding yours," <<he>> says, and lays the hand out on the table with the palm turned up.
You finish the drawing that way. Kylar looks from the page to <<his>> own hand, then closes it.
<br><br>
<<link [[Put the drawings away|Kylar Autism Return]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Training Choice
<<effects>><<set _focus to autismKylarTrainingFocus()>>
You list the places where you could work on <span class="gold"><<= autismKylarTrainingName()>></span>.
Kylar repeats them back in the order you said them, working out the walk to each one before <<he>> answers.
<br><br>
<<if ["physique", "athletics", "brawling", "footwork", "striking", "kicking", "willpower"].includes(_focus)>>
	<<if Time.hour gte 8 and Time.hour lt 21>>
		<<mmagymicon>><<link [[Go to the gym together (0:20)|Kylar Autism Gym]]>><<pass 20>><</link>>
	<<else>>
		<<mmagymicon>><span class="blue">The gym is shut at this hour.</span>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if ["swimming", "athletics", "willpower"].includes(_focus)>>
	<<beachicon>><<link [[Go to the beach together (0:25)|Kylar Autism Beach]]>><<pass 25>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if ["athletics", "dancing", "tending", "willpower"].includes(_focus)>>
	<<parkicon>><<link [[Go to the park together (0:15)|Kylar Autism Park]]>><<pass 15>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if ["science", "maths", "english", "history", "housekeeping"].includes(_focus)>>
	<<homeicon>><<link [[Go to the orphanage together (0:15)|Kylar Autism Orphanage]]>><<pass 15>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Stay here|Kylar Autism Training Decline]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Gym
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "mma_gym">><<effects>>
Kylar comes through the door a step behind you and catches the back of your shoe.
Somewhere past the reception desk a weight goes down on the floor, and the sound carries through it.
<<His>> hand closes on your sleeve.
<br><br>
"What was that," <<he>> says. It isn't a question until you look at <<him>>. "Where did it come from?"
<br><br>
You point out the doorway it came through. Kylar looks at the doorway for a few seconds,
then lets go of your sleeve. <<He>> keeps <<his>> shoulder against the wall as you cross the floor,
and only steps away from it at the racks.
<br><br>
"Which one am I meant to take?" <<he>> asks.
<br><br>
You pick out a light dumbbell and show <<him>> the movement. Kylar isn't watching your hands.
<<He>> has both of <<his>> around the handle of the one next to it, and <<he>> pulls until <<his>> forearms
shake and the bar stays where it is. <<He>> checks underneath it, as though it might be fixed to the rack.
<br><br>
"That one's too heavy for you," you say.
<br><br>
Kylar lets go and wipes both palms on <<his>> clothes. "I knew that. I wanted to see whether you did."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Kylar Autism Gym 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Gym 2
<<effects>>
<<set _focus to autismKylarTrainingFocus()>>
<<if ["brawling", "footwork", "striking", "kicking", "willpower"].includes(_focus)>>
	You take <<him>> over to the mats and set <<his>> feet where you want them.
	Kylar looks down at them, then at yours, then back at <<his>> own to check they haven't moved since <<he>> last looked.
<<elseif _focus is "athletics">>
	You take the two treadmills at the end of the row. Kylar reads the panel on <<his>> twice,
	then waits with one hand on the rail for you to start yours first.
<<else>>
	You put two workable weights on the floor with space around them. Kylar stands off to the side,
	moving from one foot to the other, waiting to be told what happens next.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Start the session (1:00)|Kylar Autism Gym Training]]>><<pass 60>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave before training|Kylar Autism Leave]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Gym Training
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "mma_gym">><<effects>>
<<set _focus to autismKylarTrainingFocus()>>
<<if _focus is "physique">>
	Kylar picks up the heavier of the two weights. <<His>> first set turns <<his>> wrists over halfway
	through, so you take it off <<him>> and hand <<him>> the other one. <<He>> tells you <<he>> doesn't
	need it, then takes it anyway and copies your grip without being asked a second time.
	<br><br>
	You work through your own sets between <<his>>, counting out loud so <<he>> has something to follow.
	<br><br>
	By the last set <<his>> arms are shaking enough that you slow the count, and <<he>> gets the weight
	down to the floor under control rather than dropping it.
<<elseif _focus is "athletics">>
	You start your belt at a pace you can hold. Kylar puts <<his>> straight up to match it,
	loses the rhythm inside twenty seconds and grabs the rails.
	<br><br>
	You slow both machines down and get <<him>> to take shorter steps.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> spends the next few minutes watching your feet instead of <<his>> own, which works,
	so you leave <<him>> to it. The belt stops thumping under <<him>> after a while, and you put the
	speed back up in steps small enough that <<he>> doesn't notice each one.
<<else>>
	Kylar holds the stance while you fetch a pad from the rack and hold it up at the height you want
	<<him>> to hit.
	<br><br>
	That gives <<him>> something to aim at, and something else to check first. <<He>> looks at where
	your arm is before every strike, so the drill breaks into single hits with long gaps between them.
	<br><br>
	You tell <<him>> to keep going until you drop the pad. <<He>> works through the whole sequence
	without looking up once, and the last hit moves your arm back further than the first did.
<</if>>
<<include "Kylar Autism Training Reward">>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Kylar Autism Gym Training 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Gym Training 2
<<effects>>
Kylar sits down on the bench and drinks half a bottle of water without taking it off <<his>> mouth.
<br><br>
"Are you coming home after this?" <<he>> asks, once <<he>> has the breath for it.
"I can't leave you in here. Somebody else will offer to show you how to do it."
<br><br>
You gather your things. Kylar puts the light dumbbell back on the rack and sets it square against the
one <<he>> couldn't lift, then walks out at your shoulder.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Kylar Autism Return]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Beach
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "beach">><<effects>>
Kylar stops where the path runs out onto the sand. There are no walls out here and nothing behind <<him>>,
and <<he>> stands still long enough that you have to say <<his>> name.
<br><br>
"How many people are in the water?" <<he>> asks, then counts them <<himself>> before you can answer.
<br><br>
<<He>> carries the bag further up the beach, away from a couple lying near the tideline,
and puts it down where <<he>> can see both the water and the path at once.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Kylar Autism Beach 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Beach 2
<<effects>>
<<set _focus to autismKylarTrainingFocus()>>
<<if _focus is "swimming">>
	You walk down into the water. Kylar follows until it comes over <<his>> knees, then takes hold of your wrist.
	<br><br>
	"Tell me before you go under," <<he>> says. You show <<him>> the stretch you mean to swim and the line back to the bag,
	and <<he>> makes you point at both of them twice before <<he>> lets go.
<<elseif _focus is "athletics">>
	You explain that wet sand takes something out of every step, which is the point.
	<br><br>
	Kylar presses one shoe into it and watches the print fill in. <<He>> scrapes a starting line with <<his>> heel,
	then walks twenty paces and scrapes another.
<<else>>
	You tell <<him>> you want to stay in the cold water instead of coming straight back out of it.
	Kylar puts two fingers in, takes them out, dries them on <<his>> sleeve, and asks how long each go
	is meant to last.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> wants the number before you start, so you give <<him>> one.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Begin practising (1:00)|Kylar Autism Beach Training]]>><<pass 60>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave before training|Kylar Autism Leave]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Beach Training
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "beach">><<effects>>
<<set _focus to autismKylarTrainingFocus()>>
<<if _focus is "swimming">>
	You start inside the stretch you pointed out to <<him>>, close to shore. Kylar lifts <<his>> head
	out of the water after every second stroke to find you, so you swim beside <<him>> instead of ahead,
	and that stops.
	<br><br>
	You show <<him>> how to turn without putting <<his>> feet down. <<He>> takes a mouthful of water on
	the first try and coughs it out against your shoulder, then goes straight back and does it again.
	<br><br>
	The second turn is slow and clumsy, and <<he>> finishes it.
<<elseif _focus is "athletics">>
	You run between the two lines Kylar scraped in the sand.
	<br><br>
	<<He>> goes off far too fast on the first length
	and has nothing left by the turn, so you shorten the course and set a pace <<he>> can actually hold.
	After four or five lengths you stretch it out again.
	<br><br>
	By the end <<he>> is turning when you turn, rather than chasing you back down the beach.
<<else>>
	You walk in together on the count you gave <<him>>, saying the numbers out loud.
	<br><br>
	Kylar starts trying to leave when the water reaches <<his>> waist, so you keep
	counting at the same speed and don't move. <<He>> stays. On the next go <<he>> gets to the end
	of the count without pulling at your arm, and comes out when you do instead of before you.
<</if>>
<<include "Kylar Autism Training Reward">>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Kylar Autism Beach Training 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Beach Training 2
<<effects>>
You collect your things from beside the bag. Kylar brushes sand off the back of your clothes,
then keeps brushing the same patch until you move <<his>> hand.
<br><br>
On the way up the path <<he>> takes the side nearest the road and looks back whenever you drop more than a step behind.
<br><br>
<<link [[Walk back with Kylar|Kylar Autism Return]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Park
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "park">><<effects>>
<<set _focus to autismKylarTrainingFocus()>>
You find a clear stretch of grass off the main path. Kylar walks the edge of it before <<he>> sits,
and picks the spot with a hedge at <<his>> back.
<br><br>
Someone jogs past behind the hedge anyway. Kylar turns to look, finds nothing, and turns back.
It happens twice more in the next few minutes, and each time <<he>> loses whatever <<he>> was saying.
<br><br>
"I can't hear which ones are coming closer," <<he>> says. You move so you are facing the path and
<<he>> is facing you, and tell <<him>> you'll say something if anyone stops. After that <<he>> only turns once.
<br><br>
<<switch _focus>>
	<<case "athletics">>You walk a route through the trees and around the benches so <<he>> knows where it goes. Kylar points out two roots that stick up out of the grass and stands on the second one to prove it.
	<<case "willpower">>The sheltered spot is the wrong one for this, so you move to the bench nearest the busy path and tell <<him>> the point is to keep working while people go by. Kylar looks back at the hedge you have just left, then writes the task at the top of a page with the finish time under it, and turns it so you can both read it.
	<<case "dancing">>You take <<him>> through the steps at half speed. Kylar counts them under <<his>> breath and stops dead every time your foot lands somewhere <<he>> wasn't expecting.
	<<case "tending">>The bed you want is a little further along, so you leave the grass for it. You kneel and work out which plants are being crowded, and Kylar puts <<himself>> between you and the path before <<he>> looks at anything else. <<He>> holds a leaf next to another leaf before <<he>> lets you pull one out.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Begin practising (1:00)|Kylar Autism Park Training]]>><<pass 60>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave before training|Kylar Autism Leave]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Park Training
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "park">><<effects>>
<<set _focus to autismKylarTrainingFocus()>>
<<switch _focus>>
	<<case "athletics">>You run the route together. Kylar calls out both roots on the first lap, then a bench, then a bin, and by the third lap <<he>> is too short of breath to finish. You ask <<him>> to save it for anything that has actually changed. <<He>> says nothing at all for the next two laps, which is its own problem, and then starts calling the wet patches.<br><br>By the last lap <<he>> is running level with you instead of talking over <<his>> shoulder.
	<<case "willpower">>You work down the page while shoes scrape past and a group of children run the length of the path twice. Kylar loses <<his>> line every time somebody slows down near you. You tap the word <<he>> stopped at so <<he>> can pick it up without going back to the top, and after the third time <<he>> starts doing the same for you when your head comes up.
	<<case "dancing">>You go through the short routine until Kylar stops watching only your feet. <<He>> misses the turn when your shoulder brushes <<his>>, steps back into place and picks the count up where it was. The next three turns hold.
	<<case "tending">>You break up the soil while Kylar sorts what comes out. <<He>> asks you to check the first few, then stops asking and starts showing you each root before <<he>> puts the weed on the pile. The bed has straight rows in it by the time you stand up.
<</switch>>
<<include "Kylar Autism Training Reward">>
<br><br>
Kylar walks the edge of the grass once more before <<he>> follows you onto the path,
and takes the side nearest the road without saying anything about it.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Kylar Autism Return]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Orphanage
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<set _focus to autismKylarTrainingFocus()>>
Kylar stops inside the door. "Is Bailey in?" <<he>> asks, and doesn't move until you answer.
<br><br>
You tell <<him>> where Bailey will be, and that nobody comes through this room on the way to anywhere.
Kylar takes a moment with that, then follows you to a table and sits in the chair facing the door,
leaving you the one against the wall.
<br><br>
Two orphans come over before you have anything on the table, and a third leans on the back of Kylar's
chair to see what <<he>> is holding. Kylar goes still with both arms over the sketchbook.
<br><br>
You hand the nearest one a spare pencil and tell them the table is taken for an hour. They go,
and the others follow. Kylar watches the door they leave by for a while afterwards.
<br><br>
<<if ["science", "maths", "english", "history"].includes(_focus)>>
	You put the book down between you and open it. Kylar reads the contents page, finds the section you want,
	and folds the corner of the page before it so <<he>> can get back there fast.
<<else>>
	You bring over a basket of clean laundry. Kylar starts sorting it by owner, by colour,
	then gets stuck on a shirt that could go on either of two piles. You turn the collar over and show
	<<him>> the name sewn into it.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Work together (1:00)|Kylar Autism Orphanage Training]]>><<pass 60>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stop before starting|Kylar Autism Leave]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Orphanage Training
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<set _focus to autismKylarTrainingFocus()>>
<<switch _focus>>
	<<case "science">>You copy the diagram out of the book, then cover the book and draw it again from memory. Kylar spots that you have two labels the wrong way round before you do. <<He>> finds the line of text that proves it, waits while you fix the page, then puts <<his>> hand over the book for you to try a third time.
	<<case "maths">>You work the same problem two ways. Kylar writes out every line even after <<he>> has the answer, so when your results disagree you can walk back up <<his>> page together. You find it eleven lines down, where a seven became a one.
	<<case "english">>You read the passage out loud and you argue about why the two characters don't sound alike. Kylar underlines every word that appears twice, then reads the next paragraph out with those words taken out. It comes out faster, and you can hear where the weight has moved.
	<<case "history">>You lay the dates out across the table and join each event to the one it caused. Kylar moves one of your cards two places along. You make <<him>> justify it, so <<he>> goes back to the book, finds the paragraph and reads it to you with <<his>> finger under the line.
	<<case "housekeeping">>You fold while Kylar checks the collars. <<He>> starts unfolding your work to redo any fold that isn't square, which stops the pile growing at all, so you give <<him>> the socks and the small things and take the rest yourself. The basket empties without either of you starting a pile over.
<</switch>>
<<include "Kylar Autism Training Reward">>
<br><br>
One of the orphans comes back to ask whether Kylar is coming again. <<He>> looks at you before <<he>> answers.
"When <<pshe>> brings me," <<he>> says. <<He>> puts back what the two of you took out, squares the
table up behind <<him>>, and waits by the door while you collect your things.
<br><br>
<<link [[Walk out together|Kylar Autism Return]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Training Reward [nobr]
<<set _autismKylarTraining to true>>
<<set _focus to autismKylarTrainingFocus()>>
<<switch _focus>>
	<<case "science">><<scienceskill 5>><<ggscience>>
	<<case "maths">><<mathsskill 5>><<ggmaths>>
	<<case "english">><<englishskill 5>><<ggenglish>>
	<<case "history">><<historyskill 5>><<gghistory>>
	<<case "physique">><<physique 5>><<ggphysique>>
	<<case "athletics">><<athletics 5>><<ggathletics>>
	<<case "willpower">><<willpower 5>><<ggwillpower>>
	<<case "swimming">><<swimmingskilluse>><<ggswimming>>
	<<case "dancing">><<danceskill 5>><<ggdanceskill>>
	<<case "tending">><<tending 5>><<ggtending>>
	<<case "housekeeping">><<housekeeping 5>><<gghousekeeping>>
	<<case "brawling">>
		<<set _gain to 5 * autismStatGainMultiplier("brawling", 5, "training") * (($statGainMult / 100) * (1 + 0.5 * $featsBoosts.upgrades.transcend / 100))>>
		<<if $combatExtended.brawling gt 1000 or $AMCTraits.halfGain is 1>><<set _gain /= $AMCTraits.brawling>><</if>>
		<<set $combatExtended.brawling to Math.clamp($combatExtended.brawling + _gain, 0, 1000 * $AMCTraits.brawling)>><span class="green">Your brawling skill improves.</span>
	<<case "footwork">><<footwork 5>><<ggfootwork>>
	<<case "striking">><<striking 5>><<ggstriking>>
	<<case "kicking">><<kicking 5>><<ggkicking>>
<</switch>>
<<stress -6>><<lstress>><<npcincr Kylar love 1>><<glove>>
<<run autismFinishKylarTraining()>>
<br><br>

:: Kylar Autism Leave
<<effects>>
<<run autismFinishKylarTraining()>>
You tell Kylar you're not going to start after all. <<He>> looks at the spot where you were going to work,
then puts <<his>> sketchbook away.
<br><br>
<<switch $location>>
	<<case "mma_gym">><<He>> carries the light dumbbell back to the rack, and takes the long way round the man on the mats.
	<<case "beach">><<He>> knocks the sand out of both shoes against the path before <<he>> puts them back on.
	<<case "park">><<He>> walks the edge of the grass once, then follows you to the gate.
	<<case "home">><<He>> puts the supplies back where you got them and checks the table twice on the way past.
<</switch>>
<br><br>
Kylar falls in beside you on the way out. "Tell me first, next time you change your mind," <<he>> says.
"I came here for this."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Kylar Autism Return]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Kylar Autism Return
<<if $autismSpectrum and $autismSpectrum.kylarReturn>>
	<<set $location to $autismSpectrum.kylarReturn.location>>
	<<set $outside to $autismSpectrum.kylarReturn.outside>>
	<<run delete $autismSpectrum.kylarReturn>>
<</if>>
<<effects>>
<<kylaroptions "notext">>